==Strategy==
This stage isn't too bad, despite how it may seem. Gobble is a fairly trivial enemy, some decent anti-floating will take care of it. Particularly notable is [[Gold Brick Cat (Special Cat)|King Nekokhamen]], who can stall Gobbles easily if you can spare the Gold Catfruit thanks to being Toxic immune. [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and any Wave or Surge units will also work quite well for dealing damage to them once the base is hit.

[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] is also notable for blocking the Diabrollow's Mini-Waves, helping to prevent your units from being interrupted by the Knockback. Other than that, bring a shield piercer like [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] for the Midnite D's shields and some anti-Aku units, and you'll be good to go.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Death's Daughter Lunacia]]: The EPICFEST variant of Lunacia makes this stage a joke. Being Toxic immune, Weakening every enemy found here, having a chance to pierce shields, and even having Counter Surge to benefit from the Sinner Snaches's Death Surges make her the perfect counter to this stage.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Jizo's Mega-Castle/Ultra Kasa Jizo]]: Jizo's Toxic Immune talent, unfortunately only available in True and Ultra form, allows him to function well in this stage despite it lacking both of his target traits. His Ultra form even allows him to barely outrange the Midnite D.s and deal good damage in the process. Consider investing in his Surge Resist Talent to reduce the impact of the Sinner Snache's Death-Surges.
*[[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]] or [[One-Eyed Asuka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blue-Eyed Asuka]]: Either can work here, both are capable of Cursing the Gobbles to remove their Toxic. Kasli, Daughter if Chaos does more damage, and is generally better than the rest of the enemies for that fact, but Blue-Eyed Asuka is Toxic Immune and will have an easier time with the Gobbles.

